          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BMN+matrix+model"} BMN matrix model
            (
            %a{:href => "#BerensteinMaldacenaNastase02"}> BMN 02
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#DSJVR02"} DSJVR 02
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation"} deformation
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BFSS+matrix+model"} BFSS matrix model
            by
            = succeed "-terms" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            = succeed "-term." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/light-cone+gauge+quantization"} light-cone gauge quantization
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            not on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            as for the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BFSS+matrix+model"} BFSS matrix model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation"} deformation
            to a
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pp-wave+spacetime"} pp-wave spacetime
            = succeed "-terms" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+density"} flux density
            in the pp-wave
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory+vacuum"} vacuum
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#GroundStates
            Ground states:
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ⊥
                  %mi D
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D0\perp D2
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi M
                  %mn 5
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M2/M5
            bound states
          %p
            While the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BFSS+matrix+model"} BFSS matrix model
            notoriously suffers from issues with the definition of its ground state (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "BFSS+matrix+model#ProblemsGroundState"} there
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+field+theory"} classical
            solutions are configurations of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fuzzy+2-spheres"} fuzzy 2-spheres
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/giant+gravitons"} giant gravitons
            (
            %a{:href => "#BerensteinMaldacenaNastase02"}> BMN 02 (5.4)
            ,
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#DSJVR02"} DSJVR 02, Section 4.2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+M-theory+and+type+IIA+string+theory"} duality between M-theory and type IIA string theory
            become
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D0-D2+brane+bound+states"} D0-D2 brane bound states
            (
            %a{:href => "#Lin04"}> Lin04
            ).
          %p
            In fact,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} dually
            these gound states encode also transversal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-M5+brane+bound+states"} M2-M5 brane bound states
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#M2M5BraneBoundStatesInTheBMNMatrixModel"} below
          %h3#relation_to_black_m2m5brane_backgrounds Relation to black M2/M5-brane backgrounds
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-background" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pp-wave+spacetime"} pp-wave spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Penrose+limit"} Penrose limit
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/In%C3%B6n%C3%BC-Wigner+contraction"}> Inönü-Wigner contraction
            ) of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+spacetime"} AdS4
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+manifold"} x
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7-sphere"} 7-sphere
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/near+horizon+geometry"} near horizon geometry
            of both the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            spacetime
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi AdS
                      %mn 4
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 7
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_4 \times S^7
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+spacetime"} AdS7
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \times
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4-sphere"} 4-sphere
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/near+horizon+geometry"} near horizon geometry
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
            (
            %a{:href => "#BerensteinMaldacenaNastase02"}> BMN 02, Section 2
            ).
          %p
            %br/
          %div
            %h3#AsLieWeightSystemsInBMNModel Chord diagrams as multi-trace observables in the BMN matrix model
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetric
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/states"} states
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BMN+matrix+model"} BMN matrix model
              are temporally constant complex matrices which are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+number"} complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+Lie+representations"} metric Lie representations
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi V
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi ρ
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g} \otimes V \overset{\rho}{\to} V
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo =
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}=
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/su%282%29"} su(2)
              (interpreted as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fuzzy+2-sphere"} fuzzy 2-sphere
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+geometries"} noncommutative geometries
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/giant+gravitons"} giant gravitons
              or equivalently as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fuzzy+funnels"} fuzzy funnels
              of
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D0-D2+brane+bound+states"} D0-D2 brane bound states
            %p
              A
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fuzzy+2-sphere"} fuzzy 2-sphere
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rotation"} rotation
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant"} invariant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multi-trace+observable"} multi-trace observable
              on these supersymmetric states is hence an expression of the following form:
            %center
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/InvariantMultiTraceObservableOnBMNModelStates.jpg", :width => "600"}/
            %blockquote
              %p
                (from
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Differential+Cohomotopy+implies+intersecting+brane+observables"} Sati-Schreiber 19c
            %p
              Here we are showing the corresponding
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagram"} string diagram
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Penrose+notation"} Penrose notation
              for
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+Lie+representations"} metric Lie representations
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  these multi-trace observables are encoded by
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+chord+diagrams"} Sullivan chord diagrams
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              %li
                %p
                  their value on the supersymmetric states
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔰𝔲
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi V
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi ρ
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{su}(2) \otimes V \overset{\rho}{\to}V
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/evaluation"} evaluation
                  of the corresponding
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+weight+system"} Lie algebra weight system
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi w
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_{{}_V}
                  on
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %p
              Or equivalently, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi D
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat D
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+chord+diagram"} horizontal chord diagram
              whose
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation"} permuted
              closure is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              (see
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "horizontal+chord+diagram#ClosureToSullivanChordDiagrams"} here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                        %mo ,
                        %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_{V,\sigma}
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi D
                        %mo ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat D
            %center
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/MultiTraceObservableFromSullivanChordDiagramII.jpg", :width => "800"}/
            %blockquote
              %p
                (from
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Differential+Cohomotopy+implies+intersecting+brane+observables"} Sati-Schreiber 19c
            %p
              But since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/all+horizontal+weight+systems+are+partitioned+Lie+algebra+weight+systems"} all horizontal weight systems are partitioned Lie algebra weight systems
              this way, this identifies supersymmetric states of the BMN matrix model as seen by invariant multi-trace observables as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+chord+diagrams"} horizontal chord diagrams
              evaluated in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+weight+systems"} Lie algebra weight systems
          %p
            %br/
          %div
            %h3#M2M5BraneBoundStatesInTheBMNMatrixModel M2-M5 brane bound states in the BMN matrix model
            %p
              There is the suggestion (
              %a{:href => "BMN+matrix+model#MSJVR02"}> MSJVR 02
              , checked in
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "BMN+matrix+model#AIST17a"} AIST 17a
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "BMN+matrix+model#AIST17b"} AIST 17b
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BMN+matrix+model"} BMN matrix model
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetric
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-M5-brane+bound+states"} M2-M5-brane bound states
              are identified with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
              of certain “limit sequences” of longitudinal-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/light+cone"}> light cone
              \-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+function"} constant
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo ×
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \times N
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix"} matrix
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
              constituting
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite-dimensional+vector+space"} finite-dimensional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+representations"} Lie algebra representations
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/su%282%29"} su(2)
            %h4#TraditionalDiscussion Traditional discussion
            %p Concretely, if
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi N
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi M
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msubsup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi N
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi M
                        %mn 5
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝔰𝔲
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi Rep
                      %mi fin
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{ i }{\oplus}
                    \\big(
